                <pb facs="1272" n="1114" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1114"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Ambassador Thompson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-12-21"><hi rendition="#italic">December 21,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Answering your telegram of 18th, Secretary of Treasury says: “Transshipment of
                    goods in transit from port to port in Mexico through United States may be
                    supervised by Mexican inspectors under conditions similar to those for goods
                    coming from port to port in the United States through Mexico.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
